10
01:20:00,000 --> 01:20:06,000
Helter Skelter is a 1976 American true crime drama thriller television film based
on the 1974 book by prosecutor Vincent Bugliosi and Curt Gentry.

11
01:28:00,000 --> 01:28:06,000
In the United States, it aired over two nights.

12
01:36:00,000 --> 01:36:06,000
In some countries it was shown in cinemas, with additional footage
including nudity, profanity, and more violence.

13
01:44:00,000 --> 01:44:06,000
The movie is based on the murders committed by the Charles Manson Family.

14
01:52:00,000 --> 01:52:06,000
The best-known victim was pregnant actress Sharon Tate.

15
02:00:00,000 --> 02:00:06,000
The title was taken from the 1968 Beatles' song of the same name.

16
02:08:00,000 --> 02:08:06,000
According to the theory put forward by the prosecution, Manson used the term for an anticipated race war, and "healter
skelter" [sic] was scrawled in blood on the refrigerator door at the home of victims Rosemary and Leno LaBianca.

17
02:16:00,000 --> 02:16:06,000
It recounts the murders Manson committed, the investigation, and the 1970-71 trial, in which prosecutor Vincent
Bugliosi attempted to draw connections between the Manson family and his violent convictions.

18
02:24:00,000 --> 02:24:06,000
The 1976 film, directed by Tom Gries, stars Steve Railsback
as Manson and George DiCenzo as Bugliosi.

19
02:32:00,000 --> 02:32:06,000
Writer JP Miller received a 1977 Edgar Award from the Mystery Writers
of America for Best TV Feature or Mini-series Teleplay.

20
02:40:00,000 --> 02:40:06,000
In 2004, the book was adapted for a second made-for-TV movie, written and
directed by John Gray and featuring Jeremy Davies as Manson.

21
02:48:00,000 --> 02:48:06,000
The film explores themes of commune, historical
figure, trial, serial killer, hollywood.

22
02:56:00,000 --> 02:56:06,000
The tone is dark and emotional and intense.
